 [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1039 "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186530737 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1045 "Surface Integrals Over Cartesian Surfaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1050 900.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "55efdebf-c5f4-5896-8a96-24cfe4c710eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106057 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106057 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160836" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106057 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106057 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}12xyz\\,\\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere $S$ is defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106057 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cbfa12ab-0e88-552b-be2d-570d6151a60f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106057 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y)=1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be evaluated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}12xyz\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,12xy(x+y)\\sqrt{1+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,12xy(x+y)\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\,12{x}^{2}y+12x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12{x}^{2}y+12x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4x{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{x}^{2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\,[2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(2+2)-0 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106062 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106062 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106062 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/78/7836860694ae6246dee36a70b86bc7fcd8cf7358d47a10586ea6880759fb1588.png)\n\nEvaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhere $S$ is defined by $z=2x-y$ and whose domain is the circle of radius $2$ centered at $O,$ as shown above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106062 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "54f23aef-c157-5234-9df4-3f529af50cc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106062 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x-y)=2,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-y)=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{D}\\,({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ our domain can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, where $x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ and $y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{D}\\,({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{Δ}({r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\cdot r\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{[\\frac{{r}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{6}[\\theta ]_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{6}\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1061 44418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f07960b-27be-5aa0-93a1-7182414f7f51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1061 44419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2865c0f-bb8c-5298-b8b6-d39fcd4dd416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1061 44421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4324e02b-29a0-51f1-961f-3fecc2a25950" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1061 44429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "edfeb55c-dcca-540f-9b5b-f35820d75f59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that for a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, if a surface is given by the explicit equation $z=g(x,y)$ over a plane region $D$ in Cartesian coordinates, then the canonical parametrization of this surface is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,y) = \\langle x,\\:  y, \\: g(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad (x,y) \\in D.\n$$\n\nMoreover, we know that under the canonical parametrization, the magnitude of the fundamental vector product is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f\\left(x,y,g(x,y)\\right) \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1065 7650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "411ccf43-163d-53bb-b1f4-2b6832c905e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05c6bd5e-0a05-54b2-8760-1af815a21d72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1117310d-a59f-5c9e-afac-07ea4e950362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "181d1c26-e67d-51c2-a26a-430f785d6acb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28969ccb-d093-57d3-b212-4874bada94e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275874 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275874 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275874 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ba05209-d34b-5868-9786-58e2ff4e93bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276275 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{3}-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276275 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276275 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "58c92c9f-f7b2-5087-b5cb-9c823dd91103" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276376 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276376 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276376 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "632694f6-bc89-5